WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.980
taian biyori tenki ga ii nara kimi to

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.980
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.770
ii koto arimasu you ni ii koto arimasu you ni

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.770
I hope we have a good time together

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:15.620
kyou mo shan shan shan issho ni

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:15.620
Today let's keep

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.240
shan shan shan waraou

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.240
Sharing laughs

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:26.670
honto no onegaigoto wa kossori hiikishite kureru

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:26.670
You take care of my true wishes in secret

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:34.220
tsuitenai na tte hi no ato wa umeawase shite kureru ne

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:34.220
You always cheer me up after bad days

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:40.580
chiccha na koro kara kitto minna shitteru

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:40.580
I'm sure everyone has known it since childhood

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:49.250
sokkenai furi shinagara itsudemo tsuyoi mikata

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:49.250
You pretend you don't care, but you're always a good friend

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:58.650
kamisama wa kyou mo taihen hottokenai shoubun oisogashii

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:58.650
You have another busy day as a god; you just can't help but help out others

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:04.990
ai de minna no genki wo sotto hitonade

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:04.990
Everyone is cheered up by your love

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:13.300
kamisama to itsumo issho ni yukai ni naru otetsudai

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:13.300
I love always being together while you help others

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:20.820
daiji na egao mamorou kokoroatari aru desho

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:20.820
I'll protect that precious smile; you know what I mean

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.820
taian biyori tenki ga ii nara kimi to

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.820
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.400
shan shan moude tokidoki ikanakucha

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.400
We should go visit the shrine together

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:46.040
Oh my, this town has changed completely.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.040
I did it!

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:57.030
Yaoyorozu-dou

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:01.260
The sun's as hot as ever.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.600
I'm liable to get a sunburn.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:09.120
Memory Halation Summer

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.130
Yaoyorozu-dou

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.140
Good morning!

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:14.990
Oh, Haruka-san! Welcome!

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:16.860
It's another hot day today.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:22.530
You think it'll be unbearably hot again
tonight? It's been like this for days now.

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:27.280
It'll be troublesome if they find me; I should hide myself.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:34.040
Is that store clerk Makitarou's daughter?

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.670
She's grown quite a bit.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:40.880
Do you have any summer clearance sales?

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:44.490
Like 13 percent or 36 percent off every item.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:46.310
I told you we don't do that.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:49.890
Haruka-san, did you come here just to get stuff on sale?

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:53.890
No, I was just looking for something to buy for myself.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:56.930
Wow, this big, red asbolite plate looks wonderful!

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:01.180
Big red asbolite plate
Price 75,000 yen

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:01.190
No way! It's this cheap for an antique from the Edo Period?!

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:04.950
Look! This is a bargain right here!

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:05.610
I'm going to buy this!

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:09.020
There's a reason this item is this price.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.340
Is this a fake, then?

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:18.650
No, I promise that the item's description is true, but the painting was actually much later.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:19.760
Much later?

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:28.670
Yes, the plate was definitely glazed in the late Edo Period, but the picture was redrawn recently.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:33.300
Regretfully, I failed to notice this when I purchased it.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.960
I see, so that's the reason it's so cheap, huh?

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:38.510
I knew something was strange.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:41.670
Well, I know it's difficult to be as good as Makitarou-san.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:42.950
I am ashamed.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:45.610
Sorry for being so critical.

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:48.510
Yuzu-chan, you're still young, so it's fine.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:52.990
The item actually has a very nice feel to it, so there's no wonder you made a mistake.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:53.600
Pots

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:54.780
No need to get depressed.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:55.680
Yeah.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:59.180
Crap! I think I made her feel even more depressed!

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:03.060
That's quite the complicated matter they're discussing.

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.790
I'll take this chance to go inside.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:12.850
Anyway, where on earth is Makitarou?

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:16.820
I came all the way here to eat his dreams.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:25.510
Thriving Business

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:25.830
Is this <i>thing  sprawled out lackadaisically
on the floor a sleeping cat god?</i>

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:33.460
Oh well, I'm getting hungry. I don't really feel like
doing this, but her dreams will make a nice appetizer.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:38.030
Yurara invokes thy power; come forth, dream mallet!

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:44.060
Open, Gate of Dreams!

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:50.600
Huh? I feel like something hit my head just now.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:53.790
Oh, Mayu-sama, are you all right?

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:55.820
I'm fine; I'm sure it was nothing.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.490
Playing a fighting game with 3D graphics is amazing!

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:02.810
But, this probably cost a lot of money.

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:05.880
Oh, you don't need to worry about money.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:12.000
Thanks to you, Mayu-sama, Yaoyorozu-dou's business has thrived and we're loaded with money now!

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:16.400
That aside, Mayu-sama, what would you like for dinner?

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:17.790
Anything is fine?! Really?

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:23.420
Then I'd like some sashimi, even if it's just a little.

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:28.180
Here you go! You don't have to ask
for just a little, there's a lot for you!

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.760
Plus, there's this and that.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:37.960
Caviar, foie gras, and truffles: the world's three greatest delicacies!

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:39.690
Help yourself!

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:46.660
Mayu-sama, we have gathered a variety of the finest desserts, prepared by a world renowned pâtissière.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.600
How about some fruit?

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:52.220
The King: Durian, and the Queen: Mango.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:53.920
Melon and peach.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:55.500
Here you go.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:56.620
Please eat up.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.770
Here, Mayu-sama, open up!

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:01.300
Th-Thanks, but I can't eat all of them at once.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:05.240
Now, please eat both of these éclair pieces at once!

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.300
Those aren't sushi you know.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:11.820
This is delicious!

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:13.710
I'm happy!

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:15.440
It's like a dream.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:19.190
Now that I'm done eating, I'm getting sleepy.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:22.770
Here Mayu, sleep on my lap.

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:25.950
Mayu-sama, I'll sleep next to you.

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:29.480
Mayu-sama, I'll clean your ears.

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:32.000
This is pure happiness.

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:37.710
Mayu-sama, please eat up!

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:40.960
I can't eat any more!

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:44.830
Now that I'm done eating, I'm getting sleepy.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:46.720
Please eat up!

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:49.720
I'm totally full.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:53.180
That's freaking boring!

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:56.030
Do you do anything in your dreams beside eat, sleep, and play games?!

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:59.430
In the first place, don't go to sleep inside a dream!

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:03.590
Th-That was unexpected. Who are you?

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:07.190
You brat! Do you not even know who I am?

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.640
I will tell you only this once.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.420
I have lived for a thousand years in China,

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:15.070
for roughly a thousand years in India,

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:17.870
and for about a thousand years in Japan.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.910
I am a Baku, one of the sacred beasts,

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:23.560
and the best devourer of nightmares
in all the land, Makuragi Yurara!

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:24.970
Don't you forget it!

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:25.270
Baku

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:28.900
They are helpful sacred beasts that eat people's dreams.
However, they tend to have a big ego.

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:31.510
So, all you do is eat too.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:38.550
For starters, your dreams lacks passion and ambition.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:40.550
It also has no thrill, no suspense;

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:43.270
the hook is weak and there is no climax,

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:45.600
but the thing you lack the most is...

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:47.400
imagination!

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:50.290
What's up with this empty white scenery?!

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:53.940
You're a god, at least do something like this!

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:56.950
I'm in my house!

00:07:56.950 --> 00:08:00.830
Is that me sleeping all sloppily over there?

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:04.540
Are you surprised?

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:07.960
I'll now take you to your favorite—white scenery.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.750
How's that?

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:17.050
Why is there suddenly a blizzard?

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:20.450
Is this raging blizzard what she meant by white scenery?!

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:21.950
It's cold.

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:25.020
I see, you're cold, are you?

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:25.730
Then...

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.330
It's hot.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:31.680
Wait, I'm in the desert!

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:33.480
It's blazing hot!

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.000
I finally understand what's going on.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:42.490
I'm inside my dream and everything is
that weird nightmare eater's fault!

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:48.580
Why do I even have to deal with her bitching about <i>my  dream?</i>

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:53.180
That's disappointing. She passed out so easily.

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:55.340
What a boring girl.

00:08:57.670 --> 00:09:02.970
Now that I know it's my dream, I can control it to some extent.

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:09.980
TL Note: Sodegarami is a barbed Japanese weapon used to capture people by entangling their sleeves, used during the Edo period.

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:09.980
Her guard will be down as she approaches, so I'll take that chance to hit her with a Sodegarami.

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:14.110
Now then, I'll wake her up and take her to the next attraction...

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:15.110
Now's my chance!

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:20.820
...actually never mind. I'll leave the idiot
alone and go find a more delicious dream.

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:17.010
Uh-oh...

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:24.240
After all, tormenting her would never appease my hunger.

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:29.370
D-Damn it! You're going to pay for this!

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:31.360
Yaoyorozu-dou

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:36.360
Big red asbolite plate
Price 75,000 yen

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:39.630
Mayu-sama, Mayu-sama!

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:47.370
Thriving Business

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:42.100
Go sleep on the futon.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:45.770
I can't eat all of them at once!

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:52.540
I flustered myself in front of a customer.

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:54.620
That was a big failure.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:58.520
Moreover, I even had her comfort me.

00:09:58.520 --> 00:09:59.990
No less from a...

00:10:04.690 --> 00:10:07.520
Mayu-sama seems to have no worries.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.950
I'm tired for some reason.

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:12.920
Dad...

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:28.860
I finally woke myself up from the dream by constantly pinching the back of my hand!

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:30.400
Where is she?!

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:33.980
D-Damn her! She's casually sleeping!

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:36.570
And she's clinging to Yuzu!

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:40.410
You, wake up already!

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:43.410
What the hell are you doing, you brat?!

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.910
That's my line, you dumbass!

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:50.970
Hey, Kotetsu! Don't pick on Mike!

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:49.750
Sacred Scroll #57: Spinning Headbutt Attack!{The was unTLd, so I put this cause it's funny :D}

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:51.920
Kotetsu?

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:52.800
Mike?

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:54.860
Be nice to each other!

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:59.580
So this is the “absolute territory” everyone's talking about?

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:01.640
Maybe I'll try it.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:04.230
Be nice to each other!

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:05.500
Kotetsu?

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:07.100
Mike?

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:12.820
It seems as if we appear to her as her pet cats.

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:14.740
Now, make up with each other!

00:11:15.130 --> 00:11:16.080
Huh?

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:18.580
Isn't it night right now?

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:27.720
Oh, I see! This is Yuzu's past and we're in her dream.

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:31.490
My goodness, you had to force yourself in.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:36.570
Pots

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:36.500
It seems she's having a dream about her childhood.

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:40.880
I know, Yuzu has told me about this a few times.

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:45.010
This dream takes place on a summer day
with sunflowers blooming beautifully.

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:48.640
It's a very, very sad dream about her past.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:53.220
Hey, Yuzu, wake up right now! Wake up!

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:55.760
There's no need to have this painful dream over and over!

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:59.650
It might just be a dream, but I don't want to see you be sad!

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:02.300
Kotetsu, what's the matter?

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:04.280
You're pawing at me more than usual.

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:07.490
Yuzu! Don't you recognize me?

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:10.670
I'm not Kotetsu! I'm the cat god, Mayu!

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:14.660
Yuzu, we're leaving soon!

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:20.810
Please take good care of the house while we're gone, Yuzu.

00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:23.070
We'll be back by tomorrow evening.

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:27.570
You've been waiting to go on this trip
for a while; you should take your time.

00:12:27.570 --> 00:12:32.110
Still, we can't keep the shop closed for that long.

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:35.710
Then I'll keep the store open for you!

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:37.320
That'll make our job easy.

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:38.440
Yeah.

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:40.890
Well...

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:44.370
Maybe when you're a little older.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:50.450
Yuzu, we asked Haruka-san to look after
you, but still make sure to be careful.

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:52.090
Yeah, I know.

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:54.390
Then, we're off.

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:56.680
Have a nice trip!

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:09.080
Th-The time and place suddenly changed.

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:15.030
We're in her dream, the world controlled by her thoughts.

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:20.630
Hey, Kotetsu, Miko, quit your begging!
I'll give you food in just a second.

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:25.510
Huh, the phone?

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:28.930
Don't go, Yuzu! You shouldn't pick up that phone!

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:34.770
I'm sorry, I'll give you food after I take this call.

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:43.150
Jeez, you must be starving, Kotetsu. But really, just a moment, okay?

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:44.400
Wait, Yuzu!

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:47.900
It's no use; we're in her dream.

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:51.290
It's merely a memory of something
that has already happened.

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:55.750
That's why I don't want Yuzu to dream of such a sad memory.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:13:59.960
So, that <i>was  what happened.</i>

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:03.460
I had a slight suspicion that was the case.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:07.380
No wonder I couldn't see Makitarou in the human world.

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:09.370
He passed aw—

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:10.850
Don't say it!

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:17.480
What happens if I don't say it?
Does it undo her parents' death?

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:21.310
Shut it, you useless dream thief!

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:26.230
You sound all high and mighty, but is passively watching people's misfortunes all you can do?!

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:31.620
If you're actually the Baku you say you
are, stop Yuzu's nightmare right now!

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:40.330
Say, Cat God,

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:43.960
do you know why people dream?

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:53.350
The way people see both happy and sad
memories in their dreams is the same.

00:14:54.220 --> 00:15:03.620
When people dream, their experiences are crystallized into memories, one by one.

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:12.490
That's why I can't just erase painful nightmares.

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:17.100
You useless Baku.

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:20.610
Hello.

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:22.490
Oh, Dad?

00:15:23.350 --> 00:15:27.190
Oh, Yuzu, do you remember our promise from back then?

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:29.350
Our promise from back then?

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:31.630
Yes, the Christmas present.

00:15:31.850 --> 00:15:33.720
Yeah, I remember it!

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:37.120
TL Note: Kakiemon is a type of porcelain known for the ‘red paint' enamel decoration.

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:37.120
Here's a Kakiemon with it's red paint,

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:39.510
TL Note: Katou Toukurou was a potter recognized for his Oribe, a style of pottery originating from Furuta Oribe.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:39.510
and this one's an Oribe by Toukurou.

00:15:40.810 --> 00:15:44.300
What do you say, Yuzu?
Aren't these new items great?

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:45.320
Yeah!

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:50.740
If you like any of these, I'll give you one as a present for this coming Christmas.

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:51.530
Really?

00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:55.150
You look like you're having fun.

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:57.660
Wh-What is happening?

00:15:57.660 --> 00:16:01.410
This is another forgotten memory.

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:07.270
The memory of an old promise that has
sunk into the depths of her sadness.

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:10.100
An old promise?

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:12.800
I just told you, Cat God.

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:18.010
Eating a nightmare doesn't take away the sadness of a dream.

00:16:18.730 --> 00:16:28.980
It only abets those who need it in converting
painful memories to warm recollections.

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:32.570
To turn painful memories into warm recollections...

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:35.690
All right, Yuzu! Choose one.

00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:40.100
Oh my, are you fine with that promise?

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:41.740
A man doesn't go back on his words.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:44.760
Yuzu, good luck!

00:16:44.760 --> 00:16:46.040
Thanks!

00:16:48.700 --> 00:16:50.790
This one! I like this one!

00:16:52.810 --> 00:16:58.000
U-Um, don't you like this teacup better? It's larger too.

00:16:58.050 --> 00:16:59.140
Nope.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:00.610
How about this?

00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:01.430
Nope.

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:02.790
Then...

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:03.560
Nope.

00:17:04.550 --> 00:17:06.510
I like this one!

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:08.730
I think it's really pretty.

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:14.440
It sure is, and Dad did say you could choose the one you like.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:18.020
You've got good eyes.

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:20.110
You chose the most expensive one.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:22.070
Did I?

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:23.270
Let me see it.

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:30.200
This is the most expensive and precious piece in this shop, and we don't want thieves to steal it.

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:34.620
So, let's hide it inside a precious item
with the lowest value in the store.

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:38.190
I want to eat my dinner on it!

00:17:40.550 --> 00:17:42.710
That'd be difficult.

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:44.460
That'll trouble me.

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:45.510
Why?

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:48.460
I'll get nervous thinking it might break.

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:51.130
Let's put it away in a safe place.

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:55.590
But if we do that, I might not find it when I want to use it!

00:17:55.590 --> 00:18:01.300
It's all right! I'm sure you'll be able to find it once you understand the value of things.

00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:12.830
Dad...

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:20.400
Why did I forget about this?

00:18:30.230 --> 00:18:35.030
Yaoyorozu-dou

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:35.220
Are you sure you don't need help?

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:39.600
I'm a guardian of forgotten items and memories, you know.

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:43.440
Finding a lost item is a piece of cake for me.

00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:47.770
Mayu-sama, thanks for the offer, but I'm fine.

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:49.940
I think I know where it is.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:56.850
Dad would never say anything bad about others to me.

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:02.620
So, let's hide it inside a precious item
with the lowest value in the store.

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:14.850
If he said it's a precious item with no real value, it has to be something that Dad made himself.

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:20.230
There should be a pot inside here
that Dad made a long time ago.

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:27.620
I had a strange dream yesterday.

00:19:27.620 --> 00:19:30.250
A-A strange dream, huh?

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:36.430
Yes, it was about that day that I've told you about before.

00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:37.370
Yeah.

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:43.870
But last night's dream took me back
to a happy memory with my father.

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:48.630
It was about this rice bowl I had completely forgotten about too.

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:55.600
It made me feel all warm inside.

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:57.000
I see.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:02.350
That dream turned her painful
memory into a warm recollection.

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:09.190
She did stuff on her own to the very end.

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:11.900
She disappeared before I could say thanks.

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:19.840
Mayu-sama, I was told the souls
of the dead rise to the heavens.

00:20:19.840 --> 00:20:27.670
So, I wonder where the lost, forgotten memories go.

00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:33.330
Yuzu, the passage of time is no doubt merciless.

00:20:33.740 --> 00:20:37.620
People can't keep their memories forever.

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:43.750
That's why all memories eventually rise to the heavens,

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:49.200
to the Moon, and to the lunar vault guarded by cats.

00:20:53.760 --> 00:20:56.510
Mayu-san is as impressive as always.

00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:57.660
Indeed.

00:20:58.070 --> 00:21:02.270
She has a kind, considerate heart.

00:21:02.270 --> 00:21:02.920
Yes.

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:05.920
Did you tell them yet?

00:21:05.920 --> 00:21:10.070
No, it's not an easy job.

00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:12.800
I have to take it one step at a time.

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:14.920
Good point.

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:21.390
This small Kutani bowl is by Rosanjin? Is this for real?

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:21.390
TL Note: Kutani is a kind of porcelain; Kitaooji Rosanjin is well known for his ceramics.

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:22.170
Yes, it is.

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:24.300
What's the price on it?

00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:26.160
Kutani bowl by Rosanjin
Market price

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:26.260
“Market price”?

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:28.580
Yuzu-chan.

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:29.140
Yes!

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:31.040
Iga pottery

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:31.040
Kutani bowl by Rosanjin
Market price

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:32.970
You don't intend to sell either of these, do you?

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:32.870
Iga pottery

00:21:33.470 --> 00:21:35.480
That's a secret!

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:38.000
Beach House Coupon for Two

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:39.440
I won!

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:40.000
I won it!

00:21:40.450 --> 00:21:43.790
I won a beach house coupon in the shopping district raffle!

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:46.760
I won it!

00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:49.760
We're going to the ocean!

00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:51.840
The beach! The swimsuits!

00:21:51.840 --> 00:21:53.510
There might be nip slips!

